@*
    WORKSPACE LAYOUT - the shell every page renders inside.

      +--------------------------------------------------------------+
      | HEADER (sticky command bar + MODEL / DATA + 3-page nav)       |
      +--------------------------------------------------------------+
      | @Body - Dashboard | Trends | 3D twin                          |
      +--------------------------------------------------------------+

    Port of src/components/dashboard/WorkspaceLayout.tsx, class names preserved exactly - that is
    what makes the Tata Steel design system in app.css apply unchanged. (The React app is frozen;
    Blazor is the delivered UI. The page-title row was removed as duplication - the operating
    context below each page already carries coil, pass, direction and state.)

    Port of src/components/dashboard/WorkspaceLayout.tsx, class names preserved exactly - that is
    what makes the Tata Steel design system in app.css apply unchanged.

    ONE LAYOUT CONTRACT THIS MUST NOT BREAK: the routed page stays a DIRECT CHILD of
    `.dashboard-content`. The responsive rules in the stylesheet collapse the page grids to one
    column below 1280px by direct-child selector, and an extra wrapper div silently kills that.
*@
@inherits LayoutComponentBase
@using Crm04.Web.Components.Dashboard
@using Crm04.Web.State
@inject UiStore Ui
@implements IDisposable

@* The palette lives on :root and the stylesheet remaps every surface under `.dark`, so the whole
   theme is one class. It goes on the shell rather than <html> because Blazor owns this subtree and
   not the document element - and on the shell rather than an extra wrapper so nothing sits between
   `.dashboard-shell` and the page grids, whose responsive rules use direct-child selectors. *@
<div class="dashboard-shell bg-base-950 flex min-h-screen flex-col @(Ui.Theme == "dark" ? "dark" : "")">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#workspace">Skip to workspace</a>

    <Header />

    <main id="workspace" tabindex="-1" class="dashboard-content flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col">
        @Body
    </main>
</div>

@*
    MODAL OUTLET. Every modal renders HERE, not where it is declared.

    THIS IS LOAD-BEARING, and the reason is easy to miss. `position: fixed` does NOT
    resolve against the viewport when any ancestor has a transform, filter,
    backdrop-filter, perspective, will-change or contain — that ancestor becomes the
    containing block instead. `.brand-header` carries `backdrop-filter: blur(8px)`, so
    a dialog declared inside the header (the MODEL / DATA chip lives there) centred
    itself on the 128px header rather than the screen: the panel hung off the top edge
    and its `inset: 0` overlay dimmed only the header strip.

    The React app never hit this because Radix Dialog portals to <body>. This outlet is
    the Blazor equivalent, and it must stay OUTSIDE `.dashboard-shell` and outside the
    header. The section name must match the SectionContent in Dialog.razor and
    DiagnosticsDialog.razor.
*@
<SectionOutlet SectionName="crm04-modals" />

<div id="blazor-error-ui">
    An unhandled error has occurred.
    <a href="" class="reload">Reload</a>
    <span class="dismiss">&times;</span>
</div>

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        Ui.ThemeChanged += OnThemeChanged;
    }

    private void OnThemeChanged() => InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);

    public void Dispose()
    {
        Ui.ThemeChanged -= OnThemeChanged;
    }
}
